{"title":"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/8/278afa87a7dfa8e2b3f40e608884a690fb1325f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ast$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"8\" height=\"8\" /> be the symbol denoting the binary operation on the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of all non-zero real numbers as follows: \nFor any two numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da3c3753da85cd27d195aebb71e4d286fb8ceeea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a\\ast b=2ab$\" width=\"85\" height=\"12\" />. Then the one of the following statements which is not true, is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/1/80194a800e94d147de9a0d2cadaec8cf09925ab3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\ast\\text{ is commutative over }S \\qquad \\textbf{(B) }\\ast\\text{ is associative over }S\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ is an identity element for }\\ast\\text{ in }S\\qquad  \\textbf{(D) }\\text{Every element of }S\\text{ has an inverse for }\\ast\\qquad \\\\ \\textbf{(E) }\\dfrac{1}{2a}\\text{ is an inverse for }\\ast\\text{ of the element }a\\text{ of }S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"1052\" height=\"95\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/b/44b4ba1514e21cfa7a9a34471962f4bff2bfe0c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }\\ast\\text{ is commutative over }S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"222\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/9/da98493b596a2b5f5e10d448fd4e2b3cbd2e3d0e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a \\ast b = b \\ast a = 2ab\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"12\" />\nStatement A is true.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/2/462e098dc3fe5c5ab11d29759a2c91f28753d245.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(B) }\\ast\\text{ is associative over }S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"204\" height=\"17\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/a/47af5cba180e658900cb7d4484520f0144ee7be1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a \\ast (b \\ast c) = a \\ast 2bc = 2a2bc = 4abc\\]\" width=\"275\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/b/11b920aa2324dbf366b81d71d884af14baf225d7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(a \\ast b) \\ast c = 2ab \\ast c = 2(2ab)(c) = 4abc\\]\" width=\"302\" height=\"18\" />\nStatement B is true.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/e/55e7dc9c0b37088dd9449a9a2bf5647c34a4af8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C) }\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ is an identity element for }\\ast\\text{ in }S\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"295\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/f/0dff967d0cda711f1bec225e5f939fe2b30d071c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a \\ast \\frac{1}{2} = a\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" />\nStatement C is true.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/b/64b1cb738c21efc6627f65c022a481196904ab6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D) }\\text{From the previous answer choice, we know }\\frac{1}{2}\\text{ is the identity element for }\\ast\\text{ in }S.\\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"656\" height=\"38\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/0/6302ddc4e9f8caab1c5ae9188c9fdbb5fa194002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{For inverses to exist, they must evaluate to the identity under the operator }\\ast.\\text{ Thus, } a \\ast b = \\frac{1}{2}\\text{, which leads to } b = \\frac{1}{4a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"874\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Statement D is true.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/6/5c678442afc8f498d0dc22bc7fe317c6469dedd5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E) }\\dfrac{1}{2a}\\text{ is an inverse for }\\ast\\text{ of the element }a\\text{ of }S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"360\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac497d0a34eb3576f69b01ee9f168d6372c9f381.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2a} \\ast a = 1\\]\" width=\"79\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Since the identity is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, not 1, we can see that statement E is false.\n</p><p>Hence, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>-edited by coolmath34\n-fixed by DoctorSeventeen\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME\" title=\"1971 AHSME\">1971 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1971 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1971\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1971 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1971_AHSME_Problems/Problem